  I need to try descending with a character at level
17 and see how much difference it makes.  One thing
I have noticed is that some of the spell schools have
all you need all by themselves.

  Enchantment: slow monster, sleep, charm monster, cause
fear, confuse monster.  Proper use of charm monster all by itself
should make an ascension possible.  Confuse monster can be pumped
up at whenever power is maxed.  Interesting that wizards start
with basic in Enchantment but I never think to use them much.
Cause fear is a nice little lifesaver.  Sleep, with a little 
care, is almost a sure kill.

  Divination:  detect food, detect treasure, detect monsters,
magic mapping, light, clairvoyance, detect unseen and identify.  
Light just makes the dungeon more comfortable to move in.  As 
well as letting you see what's coming and use ranged attacks.  
Detect monsters, especially at skilled, is like cheating.  You're
never caught by surprise.  Magic mapping ditto.  Clairvoyance on 
demand is a nice little subset of magic mapping.  Detect food is 
the only dud in the bunch, and it still lets you practice up your
skills.  Even detect unseen gets useful in the demon's lairs for
finding traps.  

  Attack: force bolt, magic missile, cone of cold, fireball, 
finger of death, drain life.  force bolt wizards start with and 
am I glad they do.  Magic missile, what needs to be said.  Cone
of cold and fireball are great area effect weapons.  Not to 
mention cone of cold's ability to make ice out of water 
everywhere except the plane of water.  Finger of death is a 
wonderful instakill for disenchanters, mindflayers, Rodney, etc.
Drain life I've never found wonderful for attacking, but for
trimming armor down a notch to try for +5 it works a treat.

  The healing and escape schools are pretty good themselves, 
having cure sickness and extra healing, and jump, haste self,
levitate, and teleport away respectively.

  My point is specializing in just one school of spells should
be enough to ascend.  (Not that I'm planning on trying it any 
time soon.)  It would be interesting to try relying on the 
enchantment spells.  That would be a whole new way of playing
Nethack for me.

  More realistically, I could max out the attack and divination
schools and have 95% of what I use in the late game, barring
haste self.

