  I guess the real difference is that GoP are equally
effective enchanted or not, while GoD must be enchanted.

  And the secret to spell management is naming each
spell(book) as you read it.  Name the spellbook individually
with number of times read and turn it was last read: 1:2297.
Then name the spellbook *not* individually with just the turn
it was refreshed on: 2297.  Then use the "\" key to look at
your discoveries to seen when each spell was last refreshed.
It's work, but worth it.

  I've even copied the spellbook general names into an editor,
and sorted them by turn read to see which ones were coming due.
Very useful since you can *only* refresh a spell when it's within
1000 turns of expiring.


