  Yes yes yes, very important especially after you have the 
amulet.  On my first ascension I jumped past Pestilence on
the way to the first altar, and then again on the way back
without being touched either time.  And by jumping immediately
for the nearest altar I got there and then back to the middle
before the level filled up with monsters to make jumping 
difficult.  

  Same thing in the Sanctum: magic missile a path through the 
graveyard then #jump.  Get to the left side before it's filled
and #jump around the temple casting light and detect unseen.
(or use wands of light and secret door detection.)

  Granted, it's a specialized use and not to everyone's taste.
The #jump interface is clumsy as well.  But, it's also useful
on Medusa, the Castle, Ft. Ludious, Juiblex, or anywhere there's
a passive trap (trapdoor, pit, hole, beartrap, pool of water)
to avoid.

  Someone pointed out that the spell of jumping has the advantage
of being able to jump while burdened.  More important before the
ascension run.
